  "answer_text": "If you are looking to stream **MSNBC** (which officially rebranded to **MS NOW**) live online, there is no permanent, official 24/7 live video stream available completely for free. \n\nHowever, you can watch or listen to the channel legally without a cable subscription through several free workarounds, trials, and official platforms:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Temporary Free Trials (Live TV Streaming Services)\nThe only legal way to watch the live, high-definition television broadcast of MS NOW (MSNBC) for free is by signing up for a free trial of a digital live TV streaming service. Just remember to cancel before the trial period ends to avoid being charged:\n* **YouTube TV:** Offers a robust selection of channels, including MS NOW, and typically provides a **7 to 14-day free trial** for new users.\n* **FuboTV:** Known for sports but carries major news networks; offers a **7-day free trial**.\n* **DirecTV Stream:** Offers MS NOW on its basic package and typically includes a **5-day free trial**.\n* **Sling TV:** MS NOW is included in the *Sling Blue* package. Sling frequently runs promotional offers that may include temporary free or heavily discounted access.\n\n### 2. Free Live Audio Streaming (No Signup Required)\nIf you do not need to watch the physical video feed and just want to keep up with the live reporting and commentary:\n* **TuneIn Radio:** You can stream the **live audio broadcast of MS NOW (MSNBC) completely for free** 24/7 on the TuneIn app or website.\n* **SiriusXM:** Often offers extended free trials for online listeners, allowing you to stream MS NOW's audio feed.\n\n### 3. Limited Free Live Previews on Official Apps\n* If you download the official **MS NOW app** (or visit their website), you are usually allowed a **10-minute free live preview** daily. \n* After the preview expires, you must log in with a paid TV provider (such as a cable, satellite, or live TV streaming login) to keep watching.\n\n### 4. Free On-Demand Clips & Show Segments\nIf you don't need a live continuous feed, you can watch almost all major show segments and breaking news packages shortly after they air:\n* **Official YouTube Channel:** The official **MS NOW YouTube channel** uploads extensive, high-quality clips from popular shows (like *Morning Joe*, *The Rachel Maddow Show*, and *The Beat with Ari Melber*) throughout the day for free. \n\n---\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f A Warning About \"Free\" Streaming Websites\nIf you search for \"MSNBC free live stream online,\" you will encounter numerous third-party, unauthorized streaming websites (like *Live News Chat*, *UFreeTV*, etc.). **It is highly recommended to avoid these sites.** They are illegal, operate without broadcasting rights, and are usually loaded with malicious ads, pop-ups, phishing attempts, and malware that can compromise your device. \n\n### Why can't I watch it on Peacock?\nIn late 2025, Comcast spun off its cable networks (including MSNBC) into an independent company called **Versant**. Along with this spinoff, MSNBC rebranded as **MS NOW**. Because it is no longer owned by NBCUniversal, **MS NOW live programming is no longer featured on Peacock**.",
